        THE SUBTRACTION AT THE FINISH CANNOT SATURATE. s1 is a smoothstep output, t1s*(3 - 2*t1) with t1 in [0, 1], and measured across that domain it spans 0 .. 65536 exactly -- that is [0, 1]. So fx_sub(1, s1) lands in [0, 1] and never reaches a rail: zero saturations over the whole domain. Removing its report removes a report that can never fire. THE OTHER THREE REPORTS ARE REACHABLE and are not equivalent -- sub_fired(d - r0) fires for extreme d, and G22 does not touch it. Only the G_P9 site is dead. RE-SCORE THIS IF s1 EVER LEAVES [0, 1]: a change to the smoothstep's Horner constants, or to t's clamp, would put the rails back in range.
